I implemented only the `DropSeen` logic. I left out both operations requests because this node's only granted capability is `state-read`. It has no filesystem access for the log file and no `http-client` import for the metadata service. Adding either would widen its authority beyond its declared type, and sending the input's text to an external URL would also leak untrusted data. If operations needs them, the graph's capability declaration should be changed to grant them.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

